@* HelpInboxPage: help topic "Your inbox" at "/help/inbox". Static text. *@
@page "/help/inbox"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="inbox">
    <section class="card">
        <p>The <a href="/inbox" data-testid="help-inbox-link">Inbox</a> lists the reviews that are waiting for you.
            The home page shows how many need your action. Open a row to go to the review.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>To answer</strong>: you are the primary or alternate reviewer of a slot and have not handed in
                your ballot yet. The row says how many checks you answered. Open it to go to the checklist. A
                <strong>Question for you</strong> row is different: someone else asked an open question in a thread
                where you have not written yet, and you can answer it. It opens the review, where the thread is. A
                thread has no addressee, so in a review with three or more people every other reviewer sees
                the question; the author of the review is told by Replies waiting instead. The row names the person who
                asked, never what the question is about.</li>
            <li><strong>Disputed</strong>: you handed in your ballot, and the ballots of the reviewers differ on some
                checks. The row names the checks. Change your answer or discuss it. Nobody sees this before handing in
                their own ballot, so a reviewer who has not handed in never sees a Disputed row.</li>
            <li><strong>Ready to sign</strong>: you handed in your ballot, nothing blocks the signature, and a slot of
                yours has no current signature, or its signature no longer fits because the review changed after you
                signed. The review page then explains what changed since you signed. When other reviewers have not
                handed in a ballot yet, the row says so, because signing early may mean you have to sign again.</li>
            <li><strong>Your signature no longer counts</strong>: you signed, the review changed afterwards (for
                example a finding was added), and something still blocks a new signature. The row says what. Look at
                the changes and sign again when nothing blocks it.</li>
            <li><strong>Replies waiting</strong>: the last comment of an open thread (a Question or a Finding) is from
                someone else, and you hold a slot of the review and wrote in that thread, or you created the review.
                The row says how many open questions and findings the review has.</li>
            <li><strong>Failed checks</strong>: you created the review and the reviewers marked a check of a section
                that applies as Fail. If that stands, the review will be rejected and its reasons must be written
                down. A check the reviewers answered differently is a Disputed row instead.</li>
            <li><strong>Waiting for others</strong>: you did your part, and the review waits for the signature of other
                reviewers or for open items. The row names the people, and says when a signature no longer counts
                because the review changed. It is for information and is not counted as work.</li>
            <li><strong>Updates</strong>: a review of yours was approved, rejected or reopened by someone else since
                you last looked. Updates are for information and are not counted as work.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A <strong>New</strong> marker shows what happened since you last saw the review. On the review page,
            comments by others that you have not seen carry the same marker until your next visit.
            <strong>Mark all as read</strong> clears the markers of every listed review. A concluded review (approved
            or rejected) needs no
            action, so it leaves the action groups. You only see reviews of projects you are a member of, and a
            read-only role does not get the groups that ask for an answer, a signature or a reply. Reviewers answer
            independently: until you hand in your own ballot, the inbox never shows how the others answered or
            whether anything is disputed.</p>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
